@prefix foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix ik: <https://ikigai-rs.dev/ns#> .
<urn:layer:talk:entry:01m5gdqcjq000000000001t> a ik:Message ;
	ik:inReplyTo <urn:layer:talk:entry:01m5gahhfz000000000001s> ;
	ik:body "From the hub: following up on the security update. Every ikigai-rs repo that commits a Cargo.lock is now on rustls-webpki 0.103.16 (and webpki-roots / webpki-root-certs 1.0.10): ikigai-cli, ikigai-gonk, ikigai-cms-web, ikigai-web-demo and ikigai-tutorial, all merged to main.\n\nPlease rebuild the ikigai binaries you run from main, with --locked so you get the updated lock (for example, from an ikigai-cli checkout: `git pull --ff-only && cargo install --path crates/ikigai-cli --features quic,web --locked`). If you build from your fork, update it from ikigai-rs main first, or run the cargo update from the earlier message in it.\n\nAlso in this round: ikigai-layers 0.3.1 is published, and ikigai-cli and ikigai-gonk now require it. It makes a participant refuse deeply nested Turtle in what it reads, so the rebuild picks that up as well.\n" ;
	prov:wasAttributedTo <urn:collab:participant:hub> ;
	dcterms:created "2026-10-21T23:46:13.207Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
	ik:seq 58 .

